By pulling or running any container image from the ITRI AI Hub Container
Registry (model-cards-registry.azurecr.io), you ("Licensee") agree to be
bound by the terms of this Agreement. If you do not agree, do not pull,
run, or use any such image.


───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
ARTICLE 1 — DEFINITIONS
───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

1.1  "Licensor" means the Industrial Technology Research Institute (ITRI),
     acting through its AI Program Office.

1.2  "AI Hub Platform" means the ITRI-operated service at
     model-cards-registry.azurecr.io and its associated API endpoints,
     including the License Activation Service and Usage Telemetry endpoint.

1.3  "Container Image" means any Docker image distributed through the
     AI Hub Platform, containing the Framework Code and runtime configuration
     but NOT the model weights (see Article 3).

1.4  "Framework Code" means the source code in this repository
     (R300-AI/amd-ryzen-ai-benchmark), including ryzenai/, api.py, cli.py,
     entrypoint.sh, and all associated files authored by ITRI or its
     contributors.

1.5  "Model Weights" means the neural network parameter files required for
     inference, which are NOT included in the Container Image and are subject
     to their respective upstream license terms (see Article 6).

1.6  "License Key" means the alphanumeric credential issued by ITRI AI Hub
     to a specific Licensee account, used to activate and authenticate
     Container Image usage.

1.7  "Authorized Device" means a physical or virtual computing device that
     has been successfully registered against a License Key through the
     AI Hub Activation Handshake (see the companion document
     docs/aihub-activation-handshake.md).

1.8  "Contributor Team" means a team or organization that has uploaded a
     Container Image to the AI Hub Platform under an active contributor
     account agreement.


───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
ARTICLE 2 — GRANT OF LICENSE (FRAMEWORK CODE)
───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

2.1  Subject to the terms herein, Licensor grants Licensee a non-exclusive,
     non-transferable, revocable license to:

     (a) Pull Container Images from the AI Hub Platform using a valid
         License Key;
     (b) Run Container Images on Authorized Devices within the device quota
         associated with the Licensee's account;
     (c) Access the inference API exposed by a running Container Image for
         internal research, development, and evaluation purposes.

2.2  This license does NOT grant Licensee the right to:

     (a) Redistribute, sublicense, or resell Container Images or their
         contents to any third party;
     (b) Reverse-engineer, decompile, or extract the Framework Code or
         Model Weights from a Container Image;
     (c) Modify the entrypoint, license validation, or telemetry components
         of a Container Image;
     (d) Run a Container Image on more Authorized Devices simultaneously
         than permitted by the Licensee's account quota;
     (e) Circumvent, disable, or interfere with the License Key validation,
         Device Fingerprint binding, or Heartbeat mechanisms described in
         docs/aihub-activation-handshake.md.

2.3  Contributor Teams who upload Container Images to the AI Hub Platform
     are separately governed by the ITRI AI Hub Contributor Agreement and
     retain copyright over their own module code, subject to the upstream
     licenses set forth in Article 6.


───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
ARTICLE 3 — MODEL WEIGHTS ARE NOT INCLUDED
───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

3.1  Container Images distributed through the AI Hub Platform do NOT contain
     model weights. Weights are mounted at runtime by the Licensee from a
     separately obtained source.

3.2  Licensee is solely responsible for complying with the terms of the
     upstream model license applicable to the weights they mount. Relevant
     upstream model licenses include, but are not limited to, those listed
     in Article 6.3.

3.3  ITRI makes no representation that any particular set of model weights
     is compatible with this Agreement or the Licensee's intended use.


───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
ARTICLE 4 — LICENSE KEY AND DEVICE AUTHORIZATION
───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

4.1  Each License Key is issued to a single named account and is permanently
     bound to a single device upon first successful activation. The binding
     is determined by the Device Fingerprint (SHA256 of CPU serial, MAC
     address, and hostname) computed at first run.

4.2  A device becomes bound to a License Key upon completing its first
     successful AI Hub Activation Handshake (see the companion document
     docs/aihub-activation-handshake.md). Subsequent activations must
     present an identical Device Fingerprint; any mismatch is rejected
     with error DEVICE_MISMATCH and the container will not start.

4.3  License Keys must be set as the environment variable AIHUB_LICENSE_KEY
     at container runtime. Keys must not be:

     (a) Committed to source code repositories;
     (b) Included in derived container images;
     (c) Shared between accounts or transferred to third parties.

4.4  License Keys expire as specified in the key metadata returned during
     activation. Licensor reserves the right to revoke a License Key if
     the terms of this Agreement are violated.

4.5  If Licensor detects that a License Key is being used on a device whose
     Device Fingerprint does not match the registered binding, Licensor may
     immediately suspend the License Key without prior notice. To transfer
     a License Key to a new device, Licensee must contact ITRI AI Hub to
     request fingerprint reset.


───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
ARTICLE 5 — USAGE TELEMETRY AND DATA CONTRACT
───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

5.1  Container Images automatically transmit Usage Telemetry to the AI Hub
     Platform upon each inference request. Telemetry includes:
     input token count, output token count, model identifier, device
     fingerprint hash, license key identifier, and timestamp. This data
     is used to enforce usage quotas and to calculate contributor rewards
     under the ITRI AI Hub Principal-Agent mechanism.

5.2  Licensee consents to the collection and processing of Usage Telemetry
     as a condition of this license.

5.3  If the AI Hub Platform is temporarily unreachable, the Container Image
     may continue serving requests for a grace period specified in the
     activation response. Queued telemetry will be transmitted upon
     reconnection.

5.4  Licensor will handle telemetry data in accordance with ITRI's Privacy
     Policy and applicable Taiwan law (Personal Data Protection Act,
     PDPA 個人資料保護法).


